WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.700 --> 00:00:06.814
A customer calls the help line: why is my balance twenty euros?

2
00:00:06.814 --> 00:00:10.863
The accounts table has one row, and it only says twenty euros.

3
00:00:11.033 --> 00:00:15.775
It got there through five updates, and each one wrote over the number before it.

4
00:00:15.775 --> 00:00:17.020
The reasons are gone.

5
00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:19.489
Event sourcing keeps the reasons.

6
00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:22.076
The service never overwrites a balance.

7
00:00:22.076 --> 00:00:25.128
It appends every change to a log, as an event.

8
00:00:25.333 --> 00:00:26.818
The account was opened.

9
00:00:26.818 --> 00:00:28.754
A salary of a hundred came in.

10
00:00:28.754 --> 00:00:31.981
Then two card payments took thirty and forty five.

11
00:00:31.981 --> 00:00:36.112
The forty five came back as a refund, and a transfer took fifty.

12
00:00:36.267 --> 00:00:40.080
Each event is a fact in the past tense, and nobody edits it.

13
00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.640
To undo the card payment, the service appended a refund.

14
00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:45.494
So where is the balance?

15
00:00:45.494 --> 00:00:46.532
You compute it.

16
00:00:46.532 --> 00:00:51.169
Start from an empty account at zero, and apply each event in order.

17
00:00:51.169 --> 00:00:52.692
This is called a fold.

18
00:00:52.867 --> 00:00:58.275
The balance goes to a hundred, then seventy, twenty five, seventy again, and twenty.

19
00:00:58.275 --> 00:01:02.203
The fold lands on twenty euros, with a reason for every step.

20
00:01:02.333 --> 00:01:08.486
Folding the log for every question is slow, so the system keeps read models, called projections.

21
00:01:08.486 --> 00:01:11.499
The accounts table becomes one, fed by the log.

22
00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:20.660
A monthly statement is another projection of the same six events: a hundred and forty five in, a hundred and twenty five out.

23
00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.449
Each projection keeps a bookmark, the last event it applied.

24
00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:30.854
Months later, the fraud team asks a new question: show every withdrawal of forty euros or more.

25
00:01:30.854 --> 00:01:32.753
No projection ever kept that.

26
00:01:32.967 --> 00:01:36.403
Write it, and replay the log from the very first event.

27
00:01:36.403 --> 00:01:41.215
Forty five and fifty land in it, though they happened long before it existed.

28
00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:46.114
Replay is safe because the same events in the same order give the same view.

29
00:01:46.114 --> 00:01:51.013
So a projection never looks up today's exchange rate, and never sends an email.

30
00:01:51.233 --> 00:01:52.474
So keep every event.

31
00:01:52.474 --> 00:01:58.799
The balance, the statement and any view you think of later are folds you can run again from the start.
